  "what": "One entry per released compiled format version: the field paths, opcode names and capability tags it defined, and the sentence in section 9 that justified the bump, quoted from the page with its markup removed. scripts/check-format-additive.mjs holds the compiler to this file in both directions on every build: a field, opcode or tag the compiler defines that no version records, and one a version records that the compiler has lost, each fail naming it. The engine reads the same record the other way round: a table a later minor added and an earlier program lacks is read as empty (section 9.4, step 3), and tests/engine/format-minors.test.ts is driven from this file.",
  "paths": "A field path names a field from the root of the program. A dot descends into an object and [] descends into every element of a list, and a path ends where the format has no further named field: a constant pool entry, an instruction, a position triple, a declaration field and a request identity are leaves. requests[].body.requests is where the shape recurses, and the path stops there.",
